WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.075
Now the other direction.

2
00:00:02.325 --> 00:00:05.875
You’re given a position, and you have to put it on the chart.

3
00:00:06.125 --> 00:00:08.275
Follow the steps on screen.

4
00:00:08.525 --> 00:00:15.125
We want forty-one degrees, eighteen and a half minutes north, seventy-one degrees, thirty-five minutes west.

5
00:00:15.375 --> 00:00:17.225
Latitude first.

6
00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:24.775
Find forty-one degrees, eighteen and a half minutes on the side scale, and lay a straightedge level across the chart there.

7
00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.850
Then longitude.

8
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.300
Find seventy-one degrees, thirty-five minutes on the top scale.

9
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:37.700
Set your dividers from the nearest meridian to that mark, and carry that distance along your straightedge.

10
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:41.400
Mark the spot with a small sharp dot, and circle it.

11
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.700
And write the time beside it.

12
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.625
Why the time?

13
00:00:46.625 --> 00:00:49.700
Because a position without a time is useless.

14
00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.325
The boat was only there for a moment.
